  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Torch Technologies obligated $432M in federal contract funding in FY2026 to date. Torch Technologies won 24 awards so far this fiscal year, giving an average award size of $18M. Torch Technologies obligations are down 37.1% year over year. Torch Technologies has tracked obligations across recent fiscal years: FY21 $470M, FY22 $589M, FY23 $674M, FY24 $629M, FY25 $687M, and FY26 $432M. Torch Technologies is concentrated in research and engineering work: Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Biotechnology) accounts for $334M, Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) accounts for $59.2M, and Engineering Services accounts for $31.9M. Torch Technologies also holds smaller obligations in Ammunition (except Small Arms) Manufacturing and Other Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing, at $4.5M and $2.1M respectively. Torch Technologies current-year totals are partial, representing fiscal year to date obligations rather than a full fiscal year total.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2026 performance compare to recent years?",
        "body": "Torch Technologies obligated $432M in FY26, which is lower than FY25 total obligations of $687M. Torch Technologies peaked at $674M in FY23 and then saw declines to $629M in FY24 and to $432M in FY26. Torch Technologies year-over-year change for the current period is down 37.1%."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What are Torch Technologies most important markets this year?",
        "body": "Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Biotechnology) is the largest market at $334M. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) and Engineering Services follow at $59.2M and $31.9M. Torch Technologies has smaller obligations in Ammunition (except Small Arms) Manufacturing and Other Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $4.5M and $2.1M."
      }
    ]
